    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d110">

                <pb facs="0111" n="101" sameAs="frus:frus1937v05/pg101"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">715.1715/802: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Minister in Honduras</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Erwin</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Tegucigalpa</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1937-10-27T17:00:00-06:00">October 27, 1937—5
                        p.m.</date><lb/>[Received 7:47 p.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>99. The Legation has just been informed by the Foreign Office that the Honduran
                    Government accepts San José for a meeting place for discussions in the sense
                    outlined in the Department’s telegram 39, October 26, 7 p.m.<anchor n="56"
                        xml:id="d110-f1"/> If the date of the meeting is definitely set as November
                    1, Dr. Lainez with possibly two secretaries will leave for Costa Rica on October
                    30.</p>
                <p>The Foreign Office would appreciate knowing the exact date set for the meeting as
                    soon as practicable.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Erwin</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
